1.17%. The best trade reached plus 20.11% while the worst was minus 11.35%. Our AI analysis is learning

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:48.020
from valuation, discipline patterns, and adjusting entries accordingly. Imagine you bought a mix of

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:55.140
XIU and a few individual TSX names in January. Now you want to know whether your actual weights

00:08:55.140 --> 00:09:01.320
still match your targets after the recent rotation out of healthcare. Pull your brokerage statements

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:07.300
for the past three months and calculate time-weighted returns by breaking the quarter into sub periods

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:13.600
around each cash flow. Compare that number to money-weighted returns which factor in the size and

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:19.520
timing of your deposits. List every position size as a percentage of total portfolio value

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:24.500
and flag anything that has drifted more than 5% from its target allocation.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:31.680
Review realized gains and losses separately from unrealized ones, so you can plan tax loss harvesting

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:37.320
before the calendar year end. Track dividend income month over month to see whether your income

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:44.860
stream is growing or flat. Add up all fees paid and divide by average assets to get your all-in cost.

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:52.560
If that number exceeds 0.75%, the review should trigger a rebalance or platform switch.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:58.900
The biggest mistake is treating the review as a simple performance check instead of a rebalancing

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:04.560
and tax planning exercise. Always end the review with a written decision checklist.

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:10.920
Open your brokerage app, pull up the last three monthly statements, and calculate your portfolio's

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:17.860
time-weighted return for the quarter by isolating each cash flow date. Compare it to the simple total

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:26.020
return number your platform shows. Note any difference greater than 0.5%. Tomorrow we will examine how the

